VHPI: vhpiCompNameP on component instances

A component instance that no entity binds (legal VHDL: the instance is left
open) is still a region with its generics and ports, but nothing identified
the component it instantiates: vhpiNameP is the label, there is no design unit,
and vhpiCompNameP was unsupported. Remember the component declaration's name on
the compInstStmt and return it for vhpiCompNameP, so a tool can learn from the
elaborated design which components want an implementation. Applies on top of
0001-nvc-foreign-in-component-instance.patch, against nvc 1.23.0.

--- a/src/vhpi/vhpi-model.c
+++ b/src/vhpi/vhpi-model.c
@@ -456,6 +456,7 @@
    c_designInstUnit designInstUnit;
    c_stmt           stmt;
    tree_t           outer;   // the instance block itself; region.object.tree is the inner block
+   vhpiCharT       *CompName;
 } c_compInstStmt;
 
 DEF_CLASS(compInstStmt, vhpiCompInstStmtK, designInstUnit.region.object);
@@ -3255,6 +3256,14 @@
 
          goto missing_property;
       }
+   case vhpiCompNameP:
+      {
+         c_compInstStmt *ci = is_compInstStmt(obj);
+         if (ci != NULL && ci->CompName != NULL)
+            return ci->CompName;
+
+         goto missing_property;
+      }
    case vhpiStrValP:
       {
          c_argv *arg = is_argv(obj);
@@ -4655,6 +4664,10 @@
    init_stmt(&(c->stmt), t);
    c->outer = t;
 
+   // The component's name is what an unbound instance can be identified by
+   if (tree_kind(inst) == T_COMPONENT)
+      c->CompName = new_string(istr(tree_ident(inst)));
+
    // Make sure all lookups happen in the implicit inner region
    (void)vhpi_get_name(&c->designInstUnit.region.object);
    (void)vhpi_get_full_name(&c->designInstUnit.region.object);
